  <h2>How GDLauncher handles Forge</h2>
  <p>Open GDLauncher, click <strong>+ New Instance</strong>, pick a Minecraft version, and select <strong>Forge</strong> from the loader dropdown. GDLauncher downloads and installs the right Forge version automatically, no separate installer JAR, no Java path issues, no manual configuration. The instance is ready to mod within a minute.</p>

  <h2>Forge, NeoForge, Fabric, Quilt: all supported</h2>
  <p>Different mods target different loaders. Most classic mods (Tinkers' Construct, Create, Twilight Forest, Botania, Applied Energistics) are Forge or NeoForge. Modern performance mods (Sodium, Lithium, Iris) are Fabric. GDLauncher installs whichever loader you choose, and the Addons browser filters mods by loader so you only see compatible content.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Forge</strong>: Original mod loader since 2011. Largest mod catalog. Default for big modpacks like ATM, FTB, Better MC.</li>
    <li><strong>NeoForge</strong>: 2023 fork by the original team. Modern improvements. Becoming standard on 1.20.4+.</li>
    <li><strong>Fabric</strong>: Lightweight, fast-updating. Best for performance and bleeding-edge versions.</li>
    <li><strong>Quilt</strong>: Fabric fork with extra features. Compatible with most Fabric mods.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Forge modpacks in one click</h2>
  <p>Most popular modpacks are Forge or NeoForge. GDLauncher installs them whole, every mod, the right Forge version, the right Minecraft version, the right Java runtime, and the right configs. Try <a href="/modpacks">All The Mods 10, RLCraft, Better Minecraft</a>, or <a href="/guides/install-modpack">browse the modpack guide</a>.</p>

  <h2>Adding individual Forge mods</h2>
  <p>Once you have a Forge instance, open its Addons tab, click Add Addons, filter for the Forge loader, and search. CurseForge and Modrinth are searched together, most popular Forge mods are on both. <a href="/guides/install-mods">How to install mods →</a></p>
